From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:52:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: Port G16 to the v7.3 Rust APIs

- platform: Data<'bound> holds the DRM Registration (or, for probe_only,
  the SGX mapping); probe takes Core<'_> and returns PinInit<Data>.
- drm: UnregisteredDevice + Registration::new; RegistrationData carries the
  bound platform device; FEAT_* bools and ParentDevice; ioctl handlers take
  the Registered device and the registration data. Drop the File post_open
  /as_raw hook, which only served an abstraction we no longer carry.
- GEM: mappings and timestamp buffers hold an ARef to the object and walk
  its devres-cached sg_table() at map time instead of an owned SGTable.
- I/O: DevresIoMem from iomap_sized().into_devres(); MMIO through
  as_view().relaxed(). The RTKit crash buffer is a SysMem [u8] view of the
  reserved firmware region.
- RTKit: start_endpoint() already fails for an absent endpoint, so the
  separate has_endpoint() check goes.
- Module parameters return values; KVec drain(..) is drain_all().

Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
